/* ===== TRADUCTIONS ANGLAISES (P4 roadmap tourisme) =====
   Indexées par le TITRE français exact (clé). t = titre EN · r = réponse EN · a = libellé du bouton EN.
   Fiche absente du dictionnaire → l'app affiche le français (repli sûr). */
const SAVOIR_EN={
"Visa pour les Comores (visiteurs étrangers)":{t:"Visa for the Comoros (foreign visitors)",r:"For FOREIGN visitors only: the visa is issued on arrival in the Comoros (airport or port), with no paperwork beforehand — around €30–50, stays of up to 45 days, passport valid 6 months. Comorians are home: no visa needed, of course! 🇰🇲"},
"Aller à Mohéli : quels papiers ?":{t:"Going to Mohéli: what documents?",r:"NO visa is needed to reach Mohéli from Grande Comore or Anjouan: it's a domestic trip, like going from Moroni to Foumbouni! An ID for boarding, your MoheliGo ticket, and that's it. Foreign visitors simply need to have entered the Comoros legally (visa on arrival).",a:"🚤 Book my crossing"},
"Venir à Mohéli":{t:"Getting to Mohéli",r:"Two steps: 1) reach Moroni (Grande Comore) — daily flights via Nairobi (Kenya Airways), Addis Ababa (Ethiopian) or Dar es Salaam; 2) reach Mohéli: by speedboat from the south coast of Grande Comore (book on MoheliGo!) or by small inter-island plane (~20 minutes).",a:"🚤 Book a crossing"},
"La traversée en vedette":{t:"The speedboat crossing",r:"Speedboats link Grande Comore (Chindini/Ouroveni) to Mohéli (Hoani/Fomboni) in 1 to 2 hours depending on the sea and the boat. Tip: check the sea weather in MoheliGo before you go, and be at the pier 30 minutes before departure.",a:"🌊 Check the sea weather"},
"Vols inter-îles":{t:"Inter-island flights",r:"Small planes link Moroni to Mohéli (~20 min, Bandar Es Eslam airport near Fomboni). Inter-island airlines are mostly booked by phone and schedules change often — the speedboat remains the most popular option. Our WhatsApp concierge can help you plan the trip.",a:"💬 Ask the concierge"},
"Aéroport de Mohéli":{t:"Mohéli's airport",r:"Mohéli's airport, Bandar Es Eslam (code NWA), lies on the north coast, a few kilometres from Fomboni. It handles small inter-island planes from Moroni and Anjouan."},
"Mal de mer":{t:"Seasickness",r:"If you're sensitive: travel in the morning (the sea is often calmer), sit in the middle of the boat, watch the horizon, eat light beforehand. Motion-sickness tablets (from any pharmacy) taken 30 min before the crossing work wonders. And check the sea weather on MoheliGo!",a:"🌊 Sea weather"},
"La monnaie : le franc comorien (KMF)":{t:"The currency: the Comorian franc (KMF)",r:"The currency of the Comoros is the Comorian franc (KMF). Its rate is FIXED to the euro: €1 = about 492 KMF, all year round. Example: 10,000 KMF ≈ €20. Cash is king on Mohéli — bring notes and small change."},
"Changer de l'argent":{t:"Changing money",r:"Change your euros preferably in Moroni (banks, exchange offices) before the crossing. On Mohéli, the banks are in Fomboni (including Exim Bank) but ATMs are rare and not always stocked. Golden rule: arrive on Mohéli with enough cash for your whole stay."},
"Cartes bancaires":{t:"Bank cards",r:"Bank cards are nearly unusable on Mohéli (no card terminals in shops). Pay in cash (KMF), or with MVola mobile money if you have a local SIM. MoheliGo tickets, though, are paid online by MVola through KartaPay."},
"MVola — le paiement mobile":{t:"MVola — mobile payment",r:"MVola is the most widespread mobile wallet in the Comoros: you pay and transfer money with your phone. It's how MoheliGo tickets are paid (through our secure partner KartaPay). A tourist can open an MVola account with a local Telma SIM."},
"Le coût de la vie à Mohéli":{t:"The cost of living on Mohéli",r:"Mohéli is a very affordable destination: local meal 2,000–5,000 KMF (€4–10), village bungalow nights at low prices, more comfortable ecolodges for mid-range budgets. Travel press estimates the Comoros ~40% cheaper than the Seychelles for at least as much wonder."},
"Pourboires et marchandage":{t:"Tipping and bargaining",r:"Tipping isn't compulsory but always appreciated (guides, boatmen). For taxis and services without posted prices, the custom is to agree on the price BEFORE — with a smile: it's an exchange, not a fight."},
"Se déplacer à Mohéli":{t:"Getting around Mohéli",r:"A coastal road circles the island. People get around by shared taxi, motorbike or car with driver. Always agree on the price before setting off. To arrange a transfer or a rental, our WhatsApp concierge knows the right people.",a:"💬 WhatsApp concierge"},
"Téléphone et internet":{t:"Phone and internet",r:"Two operators: Comores Télécom (Huri) and Telma. A local SIM is easy to buy with your passport (shops in Fomboni). 4G covers inhabited areas, less so remote corners. The country code is +269. Tip: MoheliGo even works offline once loaded!"},
"Électricité et prises":{t:"Electricity and sockets",r:"220 V, French-style sockets (types C/E) — no adapter needed for visitors from Europe. Power cuts happen: a small power bank is a traveller's best friend."},
"Santé et paludisme":{t:"Health and malaria",r:"Malaria exists in the Comoros: see your doctor before departure (possible preventive treatment), and use repellent and a mosquito net on site. Drink bottled water. There is a hospital and pharmacies in Fomboni. If needed, our WhatsApp concierge will point you the right way fast.",a:"💬 Concierge"},
"Sécurité à Mohéli":{t:"Safety on Mohéli",r:"Mohéli is a peaceful, welcoming island — solo travellers, including women, say so regularly. Common-sense precautions are enough. The real « risk » here is not wanting to leave. 😄"},
"Météo et saisons":{t:"Weather and seasons",r:"Dry season from May to October: THE ideal period (sunshine, calmer seas, whales from July to October). Hot, humid season from November to April. Water temperature: 25–29°C all year round. Check the 7-day sea forecast right in MoheliGo.",a:"🌊 7-day forecast"},
"Décalage horaire":{t:"Time zone",r:"The Comoros run on UTC+3 (like Nairobi and Moscow): 1 hour ahead of France in summer, 2 in winter. No daylight saving here — the sun rises and sets around 6 am / 6 pm all year round."},
"Tenue et respect des coutumes":{t:"Dress code and local customs",r:"The Comoros are a welcoming Muslim country: in the villages, cover shoulders and knees out of respect. Swimwear is perfect on beaches and islets. On Friday at midday, the island slows down for the main prayer. Ask before photographing people — a smile opens every door."},
"Que mettre dans la valise":{t:"What to pack",r:"Sunscreen, mosquito repellent, a hat, mask and snorkel (the reefs are superb!), water shoes, a headlamp (ideally with red light for the turtles), light covering clothes, a power bank, and cash in small notes."},
"Eau potable":{t:"Drinking water",r:"Drink bottled or filtered water (available in village shops). Avoid tap water. Consider a filter bottle to cut down on plastic — the island deserves it."},
"Urgences et numéros utiles":{t:"Emergencies and useful contacts",r:"At sea with MoheliGo: use the SOS button in the app (boat tracking). On land: the main hospital is in Fomboni. For any situation, our WhatsApp concierge answers and connects you with the right local contact.",a:"💬 WhatsApp concierge"},
"L'alcool aux Comores":{t:"Alcohol in the Comoros",r:"The Comoros are a Muslim country: alcohol is not commonly sold in shops and is not drunk in public. Some lodges and visitor hotels discreetly serve it to their guests. Golden rule: discretion and respect — and try the fresh fruit juices instead, they're exceptional!"},
"Cyclones et saison des pluies":{t:"Cyclones and the rainy season",r:"The hot, humid season (November to April) is also cyclone season in the south-west Indian Ocean. The Comoros are less exposed than Madagascar, but not immune (cyclone Kenneth hit the archipelago in 2019). In season: follow the weather and official alerts right in MoheliGo.",a:"🌊 Weather & alerts"},
"Carburant et stations-service":{t:"Fuel and petrol stations",r:"There are petrol stations in Fomboni (and along the coastal road, supply permitting). If you rent a motorbike or head south by car, fill up in Fomboni before the road — and check with your driver or the concierge when fuel is running tight."},
"Recevoir de l'argent de l'étranger":{t:"Receiving money from abroad",r:"International transfers (Western Union / MoneyGram / Ria) work in the Comoros through banks and licensed agencies — the offer is wider in Moroni than on Mohéli, where the service goes through Fomboni's banks. Traveller's tip: don't rely on it in an emergency, plan your cash ahead."},
"Drones : ce qu'il faut savoir":{t:"Drones: what you should know",r:"Drone rules are poorly documented in the Comoros: ALWAYS ask permission locally before flying (village, authorities, and the marine park in its zone). Near wildlife — nesting turtles, whales, fruit bats — flying is discouraged or subject to the park's approval. The concierge can help you request permits.",a:"💬 Ask the concierge"},
"Jours fériés et fêtes":{t:"Public holidays and festivals",r:"Worth knowing: the national day on 6 July (independence, 1975), and the great Muslim festivals following the lunar calendar — Eid al-Fitr (end of Ramadan), Eid al-Kebir, Maulid. On those days the island celebrates: shops slow down, but the village atmosphere is unforgettable!"},
"C'est quoi MoheliGo ?":{t:"What is MoheliGo?",r:"MoheliGo is the Comorian app for sea crossings and tourism on Mohéli: speedboat booking in 2 minutes, secure MVola payment, QR ticket, official sea weather, boat tracking, tourist map with directions… and this search engine! 100% built for Mohéli. 🇰🇲"},
"Réserver une traversée":{t:"Booking a crossing",r:"Crossings tab → choose departure, arrival and date → select your boat → add the passengers → pay by MVola (KartaPay). Your QR ticket arrives instantly in the Tickets tab. Simple, fast, secure.",a:"🚤 Book now"},
"Payer son billet":{t:"Paying for your ticket",r:"Payment is made by MVola through KartaPay, the Comorian payment aggregator (100% local technology). Tap « Pay with KartaPay », confirm on your MVola phone, and your ticket is confirmed automatically within seconds. A 3% service fee applies."},
"Retrouver mon billet":{t:"Finding my ticket",r:"Your tickets and receipts are in the Tickets tab (log in with your phone number). Show the QR ticket at boarding — remember to save or print it BEFORE travel day, in case there's no network at the port.",a:"🎟️ My tickets"},
"Annuler une réservation":{t:"Cancelling a booking",r:"Open your ticket in the Tickets tab and use the cancel button, or contact customer service on WhatsApp. The earlier you cancel, the better for everyone.",a:"🎟️ My tickets"},
"L'embarquement":{t:"Boarding",r:"Be at the pier 30 minutes before departure with your QR ticket (on your phone or printed). The captain scans your code — bon voyage! 🌊"},
"Suivre une vedette en mer":{t:"Tracking a boat at sea",r:"From the home screen or your tickets, open the crossing tracker: the boat's position appears on the map (the captain's GPS position, or an estimate based on departure time). Loved ones can watch your arrival live."},
"La carte touristique et les itinéraires":{t:"The tourist map and directions",r:"Our Google Maps-style map shows Mohéli's sites with real photos: tap a place → « Directions » traces the route from your position, even offline. HD satellite view available. A MoheliGo exclusive!",a:"🗺️ Open the map"},
"Le concierge MoheliGo":{t:"The MoheliGo concierge",r:"Need help with your stay — accommodation, transport, an excursion, a surprise? Our team answers on WhatsApp. You're never alone on Mohéli. 🌺",a:"💬 Message the concierge"},
"Installer l'app sur son téléphone":{t:"Installing the app on your phone",r:"MoheliGo installs straight from the browser: menu → « Add to Home Screen ». The app then works even offline (tickets, map, guide). The Play Store release is on its way!"},
"Devenir commandant partenaire":{t:"Becoming a partner captain",r:"You captain a speedboat? Join MoheliGo: fill your crossings, automatic MVola payment collection, passenger manifest, tracking. Sign up from the login screen (captain account) — the team validates your profile quickly.",a:"👤 Create an account"},
"Le parc national marin de Mohéli":{t:"Mohéli National Marine Park",r:"Created in April 2001, the Mohéli Marine Park is the FIRST national park of the Comoros: 404 km² along the island's southern shore. Coral reefs, turtles, dolphins, dugongs… It is managed WITH the local villages — a model of community conservation praised worldwide.",a:"🗺️ See on the map"},
"Mohéli, réserve de biosphère UNESCO":{t:"Mohéli, UNESCO Biosphere Reserve",r:"Since 2020, the WHOLE island of Mohéli (« Mwali ») has been a UNESCO Biosphere Reserve — over 66,000 hectares of land and sea. It is the only island of the Comoros with this global recognition. You are travelling in a jewel protected by the UN. 🏆"},
"Les tortues vertes d'Itsamia":{t:"The green turtles of Itsamia",r:"Itsamia is one of the largest green turtle nesting sites in the Indian Ocean: about 5,000 females come to lay on its five beaches every year, almost every night! The village association organises night watching with guides. Golden rules: red light, silence, and never touch.",a:"📖 See the Itsamia story"},
"Les baleines à bosse":{t:"Humpback whales",r:"From mid-July to late October, a thousand humpback whales frequent Mohéli's waters — many come here to GIVE BIRTH. Watching trips run with local boatmen and lodges; some travellers see more than 30 in one stay. A show worth the whole Indian Ocean.",a:"📖 Whale story"},
"Les dauphins":{t:"Dolphins",r:"Dolphins often escort the speedboats and canoes around Mohéli, all year long, especially near Nioumachoua. Keep your eyes open during your MoheliGo crossing — the welcome committee sometimes shows up. 🐬"},
"La roussette de Livingstone":{t:"Livingstone's fruit bat",r:"Livingstone's fruit bat is one of the rarest bats in the world: fewer than 2,000 individuals, ONLY on Mohéli and Anjouan. Up to 1.4 m of wingspan! You can watch it in broad daylight, gliding over the ridge forests. An animal found nowhere else on Earth.",a:"📖 Fruit bat story"},
"Plongée et snorkeling":{t:"Diving and snorkelling",r:"The marine park's reefs are among the most beautiful in the Indian Ocean: living corals, clownfish, rays, turtles on every trip. A mask and snorkel are enough from the islet beaches; for tank diving, the island's certified dive school is in Nioumachoua (Laka Lodge). « Diving in unknown seas », says the specialist press.",a:"📖 Diving story"},
"Les îlots de Nioumachoua":{t:"The Nioumachoua islets",r:"Facing the village of Nioumachoua, a string of uninhabited islets with white-sand beaches, ringed by reefs — and baobabs worthy of Madagascar. A picnic on a deserted beach, snorkelling in turquoise water: paradise, Comorian style.",a:"📖 See the story"},
"Le lac Boundouni":{t:"Lake Boundouni",r:"Lake Dziani Boundouni, an old volcanic crater with sulphurous waters, has been a Ramsar wetland of international importance since 1995 — one of the archipelago's rare lakes. About an hour's walk from Itsamia, between forest and silence. A sacred place: visit with respect.",a:"📖 See the story"},
"La cascade de Mohéli":{t:"Mohéli's waterfall",r:"Hidden in the southern rainforest near Ndrondroni, a waterfall to cool off in after the walk. Access via the coastal road then a trail — ask for a guide in the village, it's a lovely encounter too.",a:"📖 See the story"},
"Le mont Mzé Koukoulé et la forêt":{t:"Mount Mzé Koukoulé and the forest",r:"Mohéli's highest point, Mzé Koukoulé, rises to about 790 m at the heart of a humid forested ridge. Hike among giant ferns, ylang-ylang and Livingstone's fruit bats — bring a local guide and good shoes."},
"Mohéli, « Hope Spot » mondial":{t:"Mohéli, a global « Hope Spot »",r:"Mission Blue (the foundation of oceanographer Sylvia Earle) named Mohéli a « Hope Spot » — a place of hope for the world ocean — praising its community-led marine conservation, a finalist for the UN Equator Prize. Mohéli inspires the planet."},
"L'ylang-ylang et les parfums":{t:"Ylang-ylang and perfumes",r:"The Comoros are nicknamed « the perfume islands »: among the world's top producers of ylang-ylang, whose essence goes into great French perfumes. Vanilla and cloves complete the picture. On Mohéli, the scent of ylang fills the paths — look for the yellow star-shaped flowers."},
"Règles d'or du visiteur nature":{t:"Golden rules for nature visitors",r:"Touch NEITHER the turtles NOR the corals, red light only at night on nesting beaches, leave no waste behind, don't collect shells or coral (forbidden), and favour village guides and associations: your money directly protects the island."},
"Requins et animaux : faut-il avoir peur ?":{t:"Sharks and animals: should you worry?",r:"Rest easy: the reef sharks seen while diving off Mohéli are harmless and shy, and the island has no dangerous snakes or big predators. The real precautions: don't touch corals or stonefish (water shoes!), keep your distance from wildlife, and swim where the locals advise."},
"La pêche à Mohéli":{t:"Fishing on Mohéli",r:"Fishing is the soul of the villages: going out by canoe with the fishermen at dawn is a magnificent experience (arrange it in the village or via the concierge). Note: in the marine park, fishing is regulated by zones — your guides know the rules, follow them.",a:"💬 Arrange a trip"},
"Fomboni, la capitale":{t:"Fomboni, the capital",r:"Fomboni is Mohéli's capital and main town: its port (where the MoheliGo boats depart), its colourful market, its great mosque and its lively seafront. The natural starting point for exploring the island.",a:"📖 See the story"},
"Nioumachoua":{t:"Nioumachoua",r:"The big village of the south, facing the islets, at the heart of the marine park. Beaches, canoes, ecolodges (including the island's dive school) and unforgettable sunsets. ~45 min by road from Fomboni — the app can trace the route for you!",a:"🗺️ See on the map"},
"Itsamia":{t:"Itsamia",r:"A small village in eastern Mohéli, world-famous for its green turtle nesting beaches. The village association (a pioneer since the 1990s) welcomes visitors and organises night watching. Community ecotourism at its finest.",a:"📖 See the story"},
"Hoani":{t:"Hoani",r:"A north-coast village, one of the landing points for speedboats coming from Grande Comore. Its low-tide reef flat and its mosque facing the sea are worth a look before heading to Fomboni (~15 min by road)."},
"Ouallah et l'ouest":{t:"Ouallah and the west",r:"Ouallah, on the west coast, is one of the gateways to the marine park — a fishing village between beaches and forest. The more remote west coast offers the island's most spectacular sunsets."},
"Djoièzi":{t:"Djoièzi",r:"Ten minutes from Fomboni, Djoièzi lines up its long beach and its fishing boats between lagoon and mango trees. The easy outing for a taste of village life.",a:"📖 See the story"},
"Miringoni et les plages de l'ouest":{t:"Miringoni and the western beaches",r:"Around Miringoni stretch wild beaches where you will often be alone in the world. It is also a gateway to the ridge forests. Route from Fomboni: ~40 min — the MoheliGo map guides you.",a:"📖 Beaches story"},
"Où dormir à Mohéli":{t:"Where to stay on Mohéli",r:"Options are few and that's part of the charm: ecolodges facing the islets in Nioumachoua, guesthouses and village bungalows (notably in Itsamia and Ouallah). No concrete resorts — authenticity as the backdrop. Our WhatsApp concierge finds the right address for your budget.",a:"💬 Find a place to stay"},
"Où manger à Mohéli":{t:"Where to eat on Mohéli",r:"In Fomboni, a few small restaurants serve grilled fish, coconut chicken and dishes of the day; in the villages, the « mamas » cook to order — often the best meals of the trip! Lobster on the beach at Nioumachoua: the great classic. The concierge can book for you.",a:"💬 Ask the concierge"},
"Les ports de Mohéli":{t:"Mohéli's ports",r:"The MoheliGo boats mainly serve Fomboni and Hoani, linking with Chindini and Ouroveni (Grande Comore). All the ports are on the app's tourist map, with directions.",a:"🗺️ See the ports"},
"La Grande Comore (Ngazidja)":{t:"Grande Comore (Ngazidja)",r:"The Union's largest island: Moroni the capital, its medina and its dhow port, and the Karthala volcano (2,361 m, one of the largest active craters in the world). It is the main international gateway — and the departure point of your crossing to Mohéli!",a:"🚤 Book the crossing"},
"Anjouan (Ndzuwani)":{t:"Anjouan (Ndzuwani)",r:"The « perfume island » of spectacular relief: Mutsamudu and its ancient medina, ylang and clove plantations, waterfalls. With Ngazidja and Mwali it forms the Union of the Comoros. Connections mostly run through Moroni."},
"Mohéli en chiffres":{t:"Mohéli in numbers",r:"Mohéli (Mwali): ~290 km² (the smallest island of the Union), around 50,000 inhabitants, capital Fomboni, highest point ~790 m (Mzé Koukoulé), one coastal road circling the island. Small in size, immense in nature. 🌺"},
"Les origines de Mohéli":{t:"The origins of Mohéli",r:"The Comoros archipelago has been inhabited for over a thousand years by Bantu waves, later shaped by the Swahili world and Arab-Persian (« Shirazi ») influences. Mohéli — Mwali — lived off Indian Ocean trade: dhows, spices, exchanges with Zanzibar, Madagascar and the African coast."},
"Le sultanat de Mohéli":{t:"The Sultanate of Mohéli",r:"In the 19th century, Mohéli became an independent sultanate under Ramanetaka, a Malagasy prince in exile who converted to Islam under the name Abderemane and founded the ruling dynasty. His most famous legacy: his daughter, Sultana Djoumbé Fatima."},
"Djoumbé Fatima, la sultane de Mohéli":{t:"Djoumbé Fatima, Sultana of Mohéli",r:"A major figure of Comorian history: Djoumbé Fatima ascended Mohéli's throne as a child, around 1842, and reigned (with interruptions) until her death in 1878. A queen in a world of men, courted by the French and Zanzibari powers, she embodies Mohélian pride. Her full story is in the Discover tab.",a:"📖 See the story"},
"La période coloniale":{t:"The colonial period",r:"France imposed its protectorate on Mohéli in 1886; the archipelago became a colony attached to Madagascar in 1912, then a French overseas territory in 1946. Plantations (ylang, vanilla, copra), stamps and colonial administration mark this period — some archives are in the Discover tab.",a:"📖 Archive stories"},
"L'indépendance des Comores":{t:"Comorian independence",r:"On 6 July 1975, the Comoros proclaimed their independence, with Ahmed Abdallah as first head of state. 6 July is now the national day. Mayotte, the fourth island of the geographic archipelago, remained under French administration — a still-sensitive question."},
"Mohéli dans l'Union des Comores":{t:"Mohéli in the Union of the Comoros",r:"After a decade of crises (including the separatist period of 1997), the new 2001 constitution created the Union of the Comoros: three autonomous islands — Ngazidja, Ndzuwani and Mwali — with a rotating presidency. Mohéli gave the Union a president: Ikililou Dhoinine (2011-2016). The island's governorate is in Fomboni."},
"Pourquoi « Mwali » ?":{t:"Why « Mwali »?",r:"Mwali is the island's Comorian name — the one found in « shimwali » (the local dialect) and in the UNESCO listing « Mwali Biosphere Reserve ». « Mohéli » is the French form. Two names, one pearl. 🌺"},
"Les langues des Comores":{t:"The languages of the Comoros",r:"People speak Shikomori (Comorian, close to Swahili — each island has its own dialect, here Shimwali), French and Arabic: the three official languages. With French you will be understood everywhere — and the slightest word of Comorian you learn triggers big smiles."},
"Le Grand Mariage":{t:"The Grand Mariage (great wedding)",r:"The Grand Mariage (anda) is THE great Comorian social institution: weeks of festivities, processions, dances and lavish exchanges that confer the status of notable. More sumptuous on Grande Comore, it also sets the rhythm of Mohélian life — if you are invited to a wedding feast, it is an honour: go!"},
"Le twarab, musique des îles":{t:"Twarab, music of the islands",r:"Twarab, festive music of Swahili origin (cousin of Zanzibar's taarab), accompanies weddings and big occasions: orchestras, powerful voices and an audience that « sticks » banknotes on the singers. Hearing a twarab on a festival night is hearing the soul of the Comoros."},
"La cuisine comorienne":{t:"Comorian cuisine",r:"Must-tries: mataba (pounded cassava leaves in coconut milk), grilled lobster, octopus in coconut, the fish of the day, coconut rice and perfectly ripe fruit. Comorian cooking blends Africa, Arabia and the Indian Ocean — spiced with ginger, cardamom and vanilla."},
"L'islam aux Comores":{t:"Islam in the Comoros",r:"Sunni Islam sets the rhythm of Comorian life: calls to prayer, the great Friday prayer at midday, Ramadan observed with fervour. Visitors are welcomed with warmth — respecting the customs (dress, discretion during Ramadan) is the finest of courtesies."},
"L'hospitalité comorienne":{t:"Comorian hospitality",r:"« We heard the sweetest voices singing Bonjour Madame, Bonjour Monsieur! », one traveller recalled. Hospitality is a culture here: people greet you, take their time, share. The most beautiful memory of Mohéli is often the Mohélians themselves."},
"L'artisanat":{t:"Crafts and souvenirs",r:"Basketry, carved wood, jewellery, spices and essences (ylang, vanilla): Mohéli's souvenirs are found at the Fomboni market and directly from the village artisans. Buying local supports the island — avoid any souvenir made from shells or coral (protected)."},
"Le football et la vie locale":{t:"Football and local life",r:"As everywhere in the Comoros, football is king: every village has its pitch and its late-afternoon matches — remember the Cœlacanthes, the national team that qualified for the 2022 AFCON! Watching a village match is a true slice of Mohélian life."},
"Pourquoi visiter Mohéli ?":{t:"Why visit Mohéli?",r:"Because it is the Indian Ocean before mass tourism: UNESCO Biosphere Reserve, turtles nesting almost every night, whales from July to October, deserted islets, intact reefs… and fewer than 400 foreign tourists a year. The press calls it « the hidden jewel of the Indian Ocean ». Come before everyone else. 🌺"},
"« Zanzibar sans les touristes »":{t:"« Zanzibar without the tourists »",r:"Travellers who know the region say it: Mohéli is « like Zanzibar but without the tourists », or « the Seychelles 30 years ago, 40% cheaper ». Same turquoise ocean, same beaches — but here, you are often alone on the sand."},
"Que faire en 2-3 jours":{t:"What to do in 2-3 days",r:"Day 1: Fomboni (market, seafront) then the road to Nioumachoua, islets and snorkelling. Day 2: a day in the marine park (deserted beaches, picnic, diving). Day 3: Itsamia — turtles at dusk and a night of watching. Tight but unforgettable!",a:"🗺️ Plan on the map"},
"Que faire en une semaine":{t:"What to do in a week",r:"The full tour: Fomboni and Djoièzi, 2 days in Nioumachoua (islets, diving), Itsamia and its turtles (+ Lake Boundouni on foot), the waterfall and the western beaches via Miringoni, forest hiking (fruit bats), and from July to October… the whales. One week, and Mohéli will never leave you."},
"La saison des baleines (juillet-octobre)":{t:"Whale season (July-October)",r:"Mohéli's golden window: from mid-July to late October, humpback whales give birth in our waters — right during the diaspora summer and the European holidays. Add turtles, fine seas and blue skies: it is THE time to book.",a:"🚤 Book my crossing"},
"Trouver un guide local":{t:"Finding a local guide",r:"Mohéli's best guides are in the villages: the Itsamia association for the turtles, marine park guides and boatmen in Nioumachoua and Ouallah, trekking guides for the forest. Our WhatsApp concierge connects you with the right guide for your plans.",a:"💬 Find my guide"},
"L'écotourisme communautaire":{t:"Community ecotourism",r:"On Mohéli, tourism belongs to the villages: the Itsamia turtle association, the marine park guides and boatmen, the family bungalows. Every visit directly funds the island's protection — tourism that does good, and wins international awards."},
"Mohéli avec des enfants":{t:"Mohéli with children",r:"Kids love Mohéli: turtles at night (wonder guaranteed), calm lagoons for paddling, canoes, fruit galore. Pack repellent, hats and a flexible schedule. And the child fare gets a discount on MoheliGo!"},
"Voyager seul(e) à Mohéli":{t:"Travelling solo on Mohéli",r:"Solo travellers describe a safe, welcoming island where you are never really alone — you just have to embrace slowness and the unexpected. MoheliGo's WhatsApp concierge is your local safety net.",a:"💬 Concierge"},
"Le tourisme aux Comores aujourd'hui":{t:"Tourism in the Comoros today",r:"Comorian tourism is taking off: about 80,000 arrivals in 2024 (+39% in one year), driven by the diaspora and Europe. The national plan « Comores Émergentes 2030 » aims to make the country an Indian Ocean reference. Mohéli, with its UNESCO label, is its nature jewel — and MoheliGo its ticket desk. 🚀"},
"Réserver un billet de traversée":{t:"Booking a crossing ticket",r:"It's easy: on the Home screen, choose departure, arrival and date → tap the big blue button → « Book » on the departure you want → fare (Adult/Child) and number of seats. Login (name + phone, 30 seconds) is only asked at booking time. Your seat is held for 15 minutes while you pay. 🎟️",a:"🚤 Book"},
"Payer son billet (MVola / Holo)":{t:"Paying for your ticket (MVola / Holo)",r:"After booking, tap « Pay online with KartaPay via MVola »: confirm on your phone (MVola or Holo) and your ticket is validated automatically within seconds. Service fee: 3%. If online payment fails, a manual backup payment is shown (MVola transfer + reference).",a:"🎟️ My tickets"},
"Retrouver mon billet et son QR code":{t:"Finding my ticket and its QR code",r:"Your tickets are in the « Tickets » tab — log in with the SAME phone number you used when buying: that's what finds your tickets. Every paid ticket has its QR code to show the captain. Tip: download or print the ticket before travel day. 📲",a:"🎟️ My tickets"},
"Annuler un billet et être remboursé":{t:"Cancelling a ticket and getting refunded",r:"Yes, as long as the boat hasn't left! Tickets tab → « ↩️ Cancel & refund » on your paid ticket. FULL refund (100% of the ticket price), minus only the MVola/KartaPay transaction fees (non-recoverable). The team sends your refund by MVola within a few days. 💸",a:"🎟️ My tickets"},
"Changer la date de mon billet":{t:"Changing my ticket date",r:"Free! Tickets tab → « 📅 Change date » on your paid ticket → pick another departure on the same route at the same fare (if seats remain). Your ticket and its QR stay valid; only the date changes.",a:"🎟️ My tickets"},
"Reçu de paiement":{t:"Payment receipt",r:"Every paid ticket has its official receipt (logo + verification QR): « 🧾 Receipt » button on the ticket, to download or print. For a stay/car deposit, the receipt is in Account → My stays → « See my deposit receipt ».",a:"🎟️ My tickets"},
"Acheter un billet pour un proche":{t:"Buying a ticket for someone else",r:"Of course! When booking, tick « For another person » and enter THEIR name (they are the one travelling). Once paid, send them the ticket on WhatsApp in one tap: « 📤 Send the ticket » button. Handy from abroad too, for family back home. 💙",a:"🚤 Book"},
"Suivre la traversée et la partager à la famille":{t:"Tracking the crossing and sharing it with family",r:"On your paid ticket: « 📍 Track on the map » shows the boat at sea. And the « 🛰️ Share tracking » button sends a WhatsApp link to your loved ones: they watch the boat move LIVE, with no account and nothing to install — perfect to reassure the family, here or in the diaspora. 🚤",a:"🎟️ My tickets"},
"Publier un statut (photo, vidéo, texte)":{t:"Posting a status (photo, video, text)",r:"Tap the first bubble « Your status » (📷 with the +) on the Home screen — NO account needed! Choose Film, Video, Photo or Text; at your first status we just ask for a nickname. Your status stays visible for 24 h to the whole community (3 statuses max per day, content checked by an AI). 🎬"},
"Louer une voiture sur MoheliGo":{t:"Renting a car on MoheliGo",r:"Discover tab → « 🚗 Cars »: vehicles from our verified partner agencies (photos, price per day, with driver). Send your FREE request with your dates → the agency confirms availability → you pay a small deposit by MVola → it's guaranteed, we put you in touch. Follow-up in Account → My stays.",a:"🧭 Discover"},
"Réserver un hôtel ou un séjour":{t:"Booking a hotel or a stay",r:"Discover tab → « 🏨 Stays »: lodges and bungalows verified by MoheliGo. Free request with your dates → the host confirms availability BEFORE any payment → small deposit by MVola → booking guaranteed. The balance is paid on site. Follow-up in Account → My stays. 🌺",a:"🧭 Discover"},
"Donner mon avis, noter l'application":{t:"Leaving a review, rating the app",r:"Your opinion matters! After a trip, the « ⭐ Rate my crossing » button appears on your ticket. And to rate the app or our services (stars + comment, like on the Play Store): the « Reviews & ratings » screen — your reviews help the whole community. 🌟"},
"Messages MoheliGo (votre boîte de réception)":{t:"MoheliGo Messages (your inbox)",r:"That's right here! 📨 Account → Messages: your ticket confirmations, departure reminders (the day before), refunds and the day's weather arrive automatically. And you can write to me 24/7 — I answer right away, and if I don't know, a human advisor takes over."},
"Activer les notifications (rappels & météo)":{t:"Turning on notifications (reminders & weather)",r:"Account → « 🔔 Notifications »: accept the permission and you will receive departure reminders, sea weather and important news right on your phone, even with the app closed. On iPhone, you must FIRST install the app on your home screen (Account → Install the app). It's free.",a:"👤 My account"},
"Installer MoheliGo sur mon téléphone":{t:"Installing MoheliGo on my phone",r:"No Play Store needed! Account → « 📲 Install the app »: the guide adapts to your phone. Android: Chrome → menu ⋮ → « Install app ». iPhone: Safari → Share ⬆️ → « Add to Home Screen ». The app then opens full screen, works offline and receives notifications. 📲",a:"👤 My account"},
"Créer un compte / se connecter":{t:"Creating an account / logging in",r:"Two ways: ① EASIEST — tap « Continue with Google »: no password ever, your phone number is asked only ONCE, and recovery is automatic (new phone? Same button, everything comes back!). ② Classic — your NAME + your phone NUMBER. Your number is your identity: always use the same one to find your tickets. Login is only asked when you book — everything else is open access.",a:"👤 My account"},
"La carte de Mohéli et les itinéraires":{t:"The Mohéli map and directions",r:"« 🗺️ Map of Mohéli » on the Home screen: ports, hotels, restaurants, beaches and sites, with place search and directions that work EVEN OFFLINE (our built-in engine). Tap a place → « Directions » for the route from your position. HD satellite available.",a:"🗺️ Open the map"},
"Carte de fidélité et réductions":{t:"Loyalty card and discounts",r:"Every paid crossing adds a 🚤 stamp to your loyalty card (Account tab). After 10 stamps: a discount voucher! Also think of the Child fare (−30 to −50%) and the « My route » alert so you never miss a departure.",a:"👤 My account"},
"Alerte « Mon trajet » (être prévenu des départs)":{t:"« My route » alert (get notified of departures)",r:"In the Crossings tab, turn on « 🔔 My route » on your usual route: as soon as a boat is scheduled on it, you are notified. No more trips to the port just to ask!",a:"🚤 Crossings"},
"Changer la langue (English)":{t:"Changing the language (Français)",r:"Tap the EN/FR button at the top of the screen: the whole app switches to English (or back to French). Toute l'application est disponible en français — touchez le bouton de langue en haut !"},
"Mode sombre / mode clair":{t:"Dark mode / light mode",r:"Account → « 🌙 Light / dark mode »: the app switches to a dark theme, softer at night and battery-friendly. Your choice is remembered.",a:"👤 My account"},
"Contacter le service client MoheliGo":{t:"Contacting MoheliGo customer service",r:"Three doors: 📨 write to me right here (a human advisor takes over if needed) · 💬 Account → WhatsApp customer service (24/7) · 🤖 the assistant in Discover. We're here for you! 🌺",a:"💬 WhatsApp"}
};
/* Fusion : ajoute te/re (+ libellé bouton EN) sur chaque fiche ; fiche sans traduction = français conservé. */
SAVOIR.forEach(function(f){var e=SAVOIR_EN[f.t];if(e){f.te=e.t;f.re=e.r;if(f.a&&e.a)f.a.te=e.a;}});
